codex
**Verdict: SHIP** — for the harness and its evidence. Every case proves what its gate claims, no check was weakened, and the V4 failure is a real app finding, not a harness flaw. The app defect itself stays open as the feature-level fix-first item.

**V1 ordering proof is sound.** `InspectionDriver` writes `sampledTime/sampleStamp` at `useFrame(…, -10)` ([InspectionScene.tsx](/C:/Users/Markimus/.buzz/REPOS/jgun-portfolio/src/scene/inspection/InspectionScene.tsx:34)); CameraRig writes `cameraSampleTime/cameraSampleStamp` from the same mutated `runtime.frame.time` ([CameraRig.tsx](/C:/Users/Markimus/.buzz/REPOS/jgun-portfolio/src/scene/CameraRig.tsx:223)). Equality is asserted on every rendered frame: all tuple sets matched (108/108, 102/102, 136/136, 138/138), playing subsets 63/64 desktop and 64/64 narrow with zero mismatches — the gates' "63/64" is run-1/run-2 counts, not a hidden miss. Paused matrices identical across three distinct stamps; programs constant over 61 post-ready frames; Play-disabled-before-ready is genuinely asserted. No vacuous waits anywhere: readiness, census, and settle waits are frame- or state-based; V5 screenshots additionally require matching render stamps and nonzero draw calls.

**V2/V3/V5 hold.** Hidden-advance is measured while still hidden; seek digests agree across reverse order, DOM slider, continuous play, and replay; endpoint holds active. Restore compares camera matrix (measured delta 0), projection/inverse/state, `scrollY`, background/fog/environment/lights/stage, refreshed scroll mirror, and trigger focus, snapshotted in the restore frame itself; stale late-byte delivery and error/retry are covered. Census genuinely warms (two cycles plus 60-stable-frame renderer wait), then checks per-cycle roots/disposal invariants plus monotonic and net growth. V5 windows are parsed from `timeline.ts` (arithmetic-only evaluation), contact gap 8.99e-7 m has ~22× margin, and pixel thresholds sit far below measured values. Tolerances are spec-authored or tighter; none were tuned to pass.

**V4 is an app defect, not gate wording.** Plan §6's gate sentence — "static fallback needs neither a working WebGL context nor CAD downloads" — treats reduced and poster together, and poster complies (0 GLB requests), proving the wording is implementable. `canvasActive = tier !== 'poster'` ([App.tsx](/C:/Users/Markimus/.buzz/REPOS/jgun-portfolio/src/App.tsx:37)) mounts SceneCanvas under reduced motion, fetching three narrative CAD GLBs; the study itself correctly goes static with no tool fetch ([RingInspection.tsx](/C:/Users/Markimus/.buzz/REPOS/jgun-portfolio/src/components/RingInspection.tsx:63)). If the owner wants a static hero canvas in reduced motion, that requires amending the plan/gate first. Severity: **Medium** (degradation-path bandwidth/accessibility gate violation; no functional breakage).

Minor, non-blocking: the `preReady` measure hardcodes `playDisabled: true` after the real `isDisabled()` check (verifier `caseOrderingReadiness`, :480), and runs targeted `:4173` production preview rather than the completion spec's `:5199` — disclosed in limitations, and both archived runs plus the current script share SHA `3ceee872…`.


